Can you explain how Polymorphic Relations work in Laravel and how they're used in this example?</s> 
Sure! 

Polymorphic Relations in Laravel allow a model to belong to more than one model on a single association. 

In this example, the `Product` model has multiple `product_type` values, each of which is associated with its own model (`Event`, etc.). 

By defining a morphMany relationship in the `Product` model for each `product_type`, and a morphOne relationship in each of the `product_type` models back to `Product`, we're able to create a flexible and dynamic relationship between all of the models. 

The `morphMany` relationship in the `Product` model specifies that a `Product` can have one or more associated `Event` (or other `product_type` model), and the `morphOne` relationship in each of the `product_type` models specifies that each `Event` (or other `product_type` model) belongs to one `Product`. 

This allows us to use the same set of relationship methods (`events()`, etc.) across all of the models, and still be able to access the query builder methods of each `product_type` model. 

It also makes it easy to retrieve all `Event` models, or all `Product` models associated with a specific `Event`.

