As you mentioned, one solution could be to manually extract the data element from the JSON request and pass it to the denormalizer. However, this can become cumbersome and error-prone as the complexity of your API and JSON structure increases.

Another approach could be to create a custom normalizer that handles the nested JSON format directly. You can create a new normalizer class that extends the Symfony Serialization group's serializer and defines a new denormalize method that extracts the necessary data and constructs a new User entity from it.

Here's an example of how you can create a custom normalizer:

```php
use App\Entity\User;
use Symfony\Component\Serializer\Normalizer\ContextAwareDenormalizerInterface;

class CustomUserNormalizer implements ContextAwareDenormalizerInterface
{
    public function __construct(private ContextAwareDenormalizerInterface $decorated)
    {
    }

    public function supportsDenormalization($data, string $type, string $format = null, array $context = []): bool
    {
        return $type === User::class && isset($data['data']) && isset($data['options']);
    }

    public function denormalize($data, string $type, string $format = null, array $context = [])
    {
        // Extract user data from the 'data' element
        $userData = $data['data'][0];

        // Call the default denormalizer with the user data
        $user = $this->decorated->denormalize($userData, $type, $format, $context);

        // Extract and process the optional 'options' element
        $options = $data['options'];
        // ...

        return $user;
    }
}
```

You can register your custom normalizer as a service in your Symfony configuration:

```yaml
services:
    app.custom_user_normalizer:
        class: App\Normalizer\CustomUserNormalizer
        decorates: serializer.normalizer.object
        arguments: [ '@app.custom_user_normalizer.inner' ]
        tags:
            - { name: serializer.normalizer }
```

With this setup, the Symfony serializer will automatically use your custom normalizer for User entities when it encounters a JSON payload that matches the new nested format.

