    }
} catch (ParserConfigurationException | SAXException | IOException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

This code uses a HashMap to store the data item names and their corresponding expression values. When a data item's `<dataitem>` tag is encountered, its name is stored in the `currentDataItem` variable. When an `<expression>` tag is encountered, the value is added to the map using the current data item as the key. If the key already exists, the expression value is appended to the existing value.

After parsing is complete, the data item map is outputted in the desired format by looping through each entry and concatenating the key and value with an equal sign. 

