It looks like the issue is with the line `XmlNode curNode = ((IHasXmlNode)curNav).GetNode();`. The `IHasXmlNode` interface is not implemented by `XPathDocumentNavigator`, which is what `curNav` is. 

Instead of using `IHasXmlNode`, you can directly cast `curNav` to an `XmlElement` and then access the attributes using the `GetAttribute` method. Here's the modified code:

<pre><code>public static IEnumerable&lt;string&gt; GetAttributes(this XmlDocument xml,
    string xpathQuery, string attributeName)
{
    var doc = new XPathDocument(new XmlNodeReader(xml));
    XPathNavigator nav = doc.CreateNavigator();
    XPathExpression expr = nav.Compile(xpathQuery);
    XPathNodeIterator iterator = nav.Select(expr);
    while (iterator.MoveNext())
    {
        XPathNavigator curNav = iterator.Current;
        if (curNav.HasAttributes)
        {
            var curElem = (XmlElement)curNav.UnderlyingObject;
            var attrib = curElem.GetAttribute(attributeName);
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(attrib))
            {
                yield return attrib;
            }
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

Note that we're using the `UnderlyingObject` property of `XPathNavigator` to get the underlying `XmlElement`. This allows us to access the `GetAttribute` method.

