To detect how fast the Android device is moving using the accelerometer sensor, you can calculate the acceleration in m/s² by using the following formula:

acceleration = √(x² + y² + z²)

where x, y, and z are the accelerometer readings in meters per second squared (m/s²).

Then, you can compare the acceleration value to a threshold to determine whether the device is moving fast or slow.

Here's how you can modify the onSensorChanged() method in your code to implement this:

<pre><code>@Override
public void onSensorChanged(SensorEvent event) {

    if (event.sensor.getType() == Sensor.TYPE_ACCELEROMETER) {

        long actualTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        if (actualTime - mLastUpdate > UPDATE_THRESHOLD) {

            mLastUpdate = actualTime;

            float x = event.values[0], y = event.values[1], z = event.values[2];

            float acceleration = (float) Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y + z * z);

            if (acceleration > 10) {
                // Device is moving fast
                mXValueView.setText("FAST");
                mYValueView.setText("");
                mZValueView.setText("");
            } else if (acceleration > 1) {
                // Device is moving at medium speed
                mXValueView.setText("MEDIUM");
                mYValueView.setText("");
                mZValueView.setText("");
            } else {
                // Device is moving slowly or not moving
                mXValueView.setText("SLOW");
                mYValueView.setText("");
                mZValueView.setText("");
            }
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

In this example, if the acceleration is greater than 10 m/s², we assume the device is moving fast and display "FAST" in the x value text view. If the acceleration is between 1 m/s² and 10 m/s², we assume the device is moving at medium speed and display "MEDIUM" in the x value text view. Otherwise, we assume the device is moving slowly or not moving and display "SLOW" in the x value text view. The y and z value text views are left empty in all cases.

