One possible solution is to use Java's built-in ZipInputStream and ZipOutputStream classes to read and write the zip files, respectively. Here's some example code to get you started:

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.zip.*;

public class MergeZips {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
    // the source zip file to merge
    File sourceZipFile = new File("A.zip");

    // the destination zip file to merge into
    File destZipFile = new File("b.zip");

    // read the source zip file and store the entries in a map
    Map<String, ZipEntry> sourceEntries = new HashMap<>();
    try (ZipInputStream in = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(sourceZipFile))) {
      ZipEntry entry;
      while ((entry = in.getNextEntry()) != null) {
        sourceEntries.put(entry.getName(), entry);
      }
    }

    // write the destination zip file, overwriting existing entries with the source entries
    try (ZipOutputStream out = new ZipOutputStream(new FileOutputStream(destZipFile))) {
      try (ZipInputStream in = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(destZipFile))) {
        ZipEntry entry;
        while ((entry = in.getNextEntry()) != null) {
          if (!sourceEntries.containsKey(entry.getName())) {
            // entry does not exist in source, so write it to destination
            writeToZip(entry, in, out);
          }
        }
      }

      // write the source entries to the destination zip file
      for (ZipEntry entry : sourceEntries.values()) {
        writeToZip(entry, new FileInputStream(sourceZipFile), out);
      }
    }
  }

  private static void writeToZip(ZipEntry entry, InputStream in, ZipOutputStream out) throws IOException {
    // create a new entry in the output zip file
    out.putNextEntry(new ZipEntry(entry.getName()));

    // copy the input stream to the output stream
    byte[] buffer = new byte[4096];
    int bytesRead;
    while ((bytesRead = in.read(buffer)) != -1) {
      out.write(buffer, 0, bytesRead);
    }

    // close the entry
    out.closeEntry();
  }
}
```

This code reads the entries from the source zip file into a map, then reads the entries from the destination zip file and writes them to the output zip file with the `writeToZip` method, checking for duplicates in the source zip file and overwriting them. Finally, it writes the entries from the source zip file to the output zip file.

