To implement this, you can create a separate view that contains any additional UI elements you want to display with the keyboard (such as a toolbar with a "next" button), and add it as a subview of the key window. Then, each time a new view controller is presented with a text field, you can set the custom input accessory view for that text field to the persistent accessory view.

Here is an example of how you might implement this:

1. Create a custom keyboard accessory view with any elements you want to display (e.g. a toolbar with a "next" button).

```
class CustomKeyboardAccessoryView: UIView {

